{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot","id":792501,"title":"Compacts & Conspiracies: The Great Reboot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-24T19:53:37-08:00","id":792501,"title":"Compacts & Conspiracies: The Great Reboot","content":"Okay, so, you've probably seen the developer's blog announcing that they're taking fan feedback on what to do with the Ashwood Abbey. Now, I doubt they're going to go for a similar revamp/reboot approach to all of the compacts and conspiracies, but I thought it'd be fun to ask:<br /> <br /> What compacts and/or conspiracies would you like to see rebooted in Hunter: The Slasher Chronicles?<br /> <br /> How would you like them to be rebooted?<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking personally...<br /> <br /> I would love to see the Malleus Malleficarium rebooted, in that I would like to see them repurposed from their current &quot;anti-vampire&quot; focus to more of an &quot;anti-witch&quot; focus. I'm perfectly okay with the organization being corrupted at its roots, but the 1st edition's rendition made little sense; everything about this conspiracy, from its name to its real-world historical ties, suggests that it should fight witches. Instead, it fights vampires. Don't get me wrong, there's definitely room in the game for a compact/conspiracy secretly being controlled by a rogue ghoul, but the Malleus Malleficarium isn't it. I think it should fight witches whilst struggling with the (probably unacknowledged) hypocrisy that they themselves may be no different to witches.<br /> <br /> I really think the Aegis Kai Doru needs to have more of a focus on &quot;finding relics&quot; than on &quot;fight witches and werewolves&quot;. At the very least, it should come with sleepwalker status, because, at present, the AKD is implied to have it out for Awakened mages when, by the rules of Dissonance/Quiescence, they shouldn't be able to touch Awakened relics without rendering them inert.<br /> <br /> The Keepers of the Source need to either be made to actually make sense or just to die in a fire. A &quot;killer hippies&quot; compact could be fun, but not a lot of players want to play someone who is blatantly wrong about reality and insists on clinging to their delusions in spite of what everyone else in-universe tells them. Being misinformed is one thing, but the Keepers require a player to totally ignore everything we know about the meta-setting to have a chance of taking their beliefs seriously, which is never a good sign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:04:52-08:00","id":792530,"title":"","content":"<b>Null Mysteriis</b> doesn't need a conceptual shift, but it needs an attentive, science minded eye to look over its writeups, one that knows that science is a method, not the body of knowledge accumulated by the method. They shouldn't read like they rush into some science-fiction hypothesis to shoehorn their findings into before they have some solid foundation to ground it on. They should remember that &quot;I don't know&quot; is not a dirty word in science, and what's important isn't getting from no answer to an answer, but carefully chiselling at the edges of the unknown to make sure, however slowly the answer might have to come, it's one that fits the facts. A little pseudoscience presence is fine, both in the form of phenomena that are pseudoscience in the real world but real phenomena in the Chronicles of Darkness, and in the form of investigators who are a little kooky and don't quite have their reasoning straight. But the pseudoscientists need to feel like authentic pseudoscientists with systems based around foundational assumptions, not movie extras spouting a little bit of technobabble. A little more attention to what they use their findings for practically wouldn't hurt either, and is probably a good bridge to forge connections between the compact and other hunter cells and organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:08:15-08:00","id":792534,"title":"","content":"Kinda want one of the less murdery compacts to get an endowment. Union, network zero, null mysteriis, etc.<br /> <br /> Also would be nice if there could be groups with endowments that are less religious/spiritual in nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:20:57-08:00","id":792538,"title":"","content":"In general, Hunters need to have more to do than just kill the monsters. Every group needs some of that.<br /> <br /> The Aegis Kai Doru have very little to do with Werewolves and could serve to do a lot more with Mummies. I'd also love to have their story moved from less &quot;a more vague version of Mage's backstory&quot; to hints of a very odd mythic prehistory that doesn't tie in a overtly with the rest of the CofD.<br /> <br /> I could write a fucking essay on the mess that is the Ascending Ones in 1e. As it stands, they can't decide which of three groups they are (drug dealers and inner-city vigilantes, heirs to an ancient alchemic tradition, or religious zealots); either blend them much, much better than they are, or else pick one and stick with it.<br /> <br /> VALKYRIE could stand to be less &quot;nuke it from orbit&quot; and more intelligence or R&amp;D focused. I would love for them to feel less like a military kill squad and to draw instead from the United States' massive espionage apparatus. They also really need to feel like a big organization; 1e had a nasty way of making every cell feel completely isolated, when VALKYRIE should have a clear command chain and support structure.<br /> <br /> It would be great if Null Mysteriis weren't treated as a complete and utter joke.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge could stand to feel more like an organization and less like a type of lone wolf badass. Give them a proper base in Milan; let characters browse the archives and draw upon retainers from generations of servitude.<br /> <br /> Please dear god let Les Mysteres actually have an identity. Either make them into Vodoun proper, or do away with them in favor of a group that actually feels like something beyond &quot;the spirit guys.&quot;<br /> <br /> I hope my favorite groups (the Loyalists of Thule, the Knights of St. George, the Cainite Heresy, VASCU) get out relatively unmolested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 12-25-2015, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:38:31-08:00","id":792546,"title":"","content":"In a similar tone to my previous post, the <b>Cheiron Group</b> doesn't need a reimagining, but its writeup does need restraint. It would be easy to focus too much on the shady secrets lurking behind the Board of Directors and the history of their endeavors, and the Cheiron Group does make a great antagonistic conspiracy, but the corebook writeup needs to dial back to where it started, as a medical conglomerate performing dubious harvesting and experimentation towards defensible ends. Spooky rumors about &quot;what's really going on&quot; are nice, but it's a plenty fascinating conspiracy if it's exactly what's presented on the surface: a workaday, banal Vigil turning the dissection of monsters into an industry, with large-scale, faceless benefits that still make a meaningful impact. What's really scary, what's really gripping and resonant, about the Cheiron Group is that it's the Vigil as a business. We look in a mirror and we're not entirely sure we like what we see. Breaking that uncertainty with too many hints of an ultimately blank agenda weakens the concept.<br /> <br /> Much less important, but I also like when the text is mindful that the Cheiron Group isn't one company but several. In my head, the Cheiron Group isn't a household name in the world of the Vigil, but its bigger subsidiaries and holdings are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T08:38:17-08:00","id":793110,"title":"","content":"I do enjoy these threads <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Keepers of the Source: They need a reason to fight whites that isn\u2019t canonically wrong. There\u2019s two ways to do this:<br /> <br /> 1) A sidebar that explicitly says by the rules in Mage they\u2019re wrong but the authorial intent was that if you\u2019re playing a Keeper\u2019s game they\u2019re correct and that draining Hallows does hurt Mother Earth.<br /> <br /> 2) Go all in on the Lay Lines. They\u2019re competent enough that they can heal ecosystems or promote peace and love by adjusting the Ley Lines. Unfortunately Witches have a bad habit of coming along to steal the fruits of their labour, or trying to stop them from filling a crime ridden neighbourhood with hope because the current set up is good for spell casting.<br /> <br /> Maiden's Blood Sisterhood: They\u2019re one of my favourites, and I don\u2019t want to change much. But the picture of their sample hunter, with the occult book (Possibly the best art piece in all of Hunter. It must go in 2E!). I want to play that character \u2013 so I would quite like it if there\u2019s one canonical witch mentioned as a mid ranking member. Definitely not a member of a Mage order or anything, her only loyalty should be to the Sisterhood otherwise it sends the wrong image \u2013 I want to play a Madden\u2019s Blood Sisterhood Witch, not a Witch infiltrating the Maiden\u2019s Blood Sisterhood.<br /> <br /> Night Watch: Put more focus on the street gang angle. When I read them they felt like they were basically The Union. Just in the African American inner cities, rather than small town America / rust belt.<br /> <br /> Null Mysteriis: What Stupid Loserman said! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru: As has been said a couple of times. The AKD needs more focus on hunting Relics rather than hunting monsters. I\u2019d drop the grudge angle entirely in favour of more focus on their mysterious origins and a grand millennia long master plan that requires them to find a set of legendary relics.<br /> <br /> Ascending Ones: I love them, and I definitely want to keep the core idea of it being an alliance of three different group: Egyptian-Hermetic alchemists, monotheistic hunters, and drug cartels. The Ringed Chain from Compacts and Conspiracies doesn\u2019t work, you\u2019d need at least 3 links per cell for it to make sense.<br /> <br /> I feel that both the Southern Temple and Jagged Creascent got a bit of a short shift. I\u2019d like a bit more on what the Southern Temple actually do other than experiment in their laboratories; and I\u2019d like the Crescent to have a bit more of an ethos and goals of their own rather than just being a tool for the other two. Alchemy is about self-transformation, but while the Southern Temple have the luxury of perusing esoteric goals like spiritual perfection. The Crescent just want to transform themselves from have-nots to haves; and they\u2019re the ones who really understand that the WoD wants people to suffer and plan to defy it with the divine power of alchemy.<br /> <br /> Cheiron Group: I\u2019d like more focus on Cheiron as a system. A set of incentives that takes good people who want to cure diseases and put food on their family\u2019s tables and makes them into monsters; as surely as implanting monster parts into their bodies does. Essentially only a small minority in Cheiron are actually evil. The slashers of course, a few bad eggs, and maybe the Board of Directors (who\u2019re preferably ordinary humans). But the doctor\u2019s kids have a rare disease, and the executives have offered funding for pet projects as a reward for the most profitable team, and so he cuts corners and cuts into innocent supernaturals. The Barret Commission can balance this with a more positive portrayal of capitalism.<br /> <br /> This may or may not be a subtle Influence (as in the Strengthen Influence effect) by whomever is behind the logo, but if that\u2019s the case the human Board of Directors should be aware of it and agree to it. IMO Hunter is a game about fighting the supernatural, now being it\u2019s pawns.<br /> <br /> Also, what Stupid Looserman said.<br /> <br /> Division Six: The only group I\u2019d drop entirely.<br /> <br /> Knights of Saint George: One of the few groups I\u2019d rewrite from scratch. I\u2019d start with a core theme of Lies to contrast Mage\u2019s themes of Truth, and I\u2019d make it so that they\u2019re a relatively positive group because that would make the contrast with mage more interesting.<br /> <br /> Les Mysteres: I like them a lot, but I\u2019d drop the controlled by the spirits bit. There\u2019s a fantastic contrast between them and Werewolves; where Werewolves are a border control and Les Mysteries preach mutually beneficial integration. I\u2019d put the focus on that conflict; and it doesn\u2019t work (nor do hunter\u2019s core themes) if the Spirits are actually in control.<br /> <br /> Lucifuge: Not much I\u2019d change. But I\u2019d drop the idea of The Denial being friendly, and The Reconciliation being kill-em-all. Instead The Denial say \u201cI\u2019m not a monster!\u201d, the Reconciliation say \u201cI\u2019m a demon, but I\u2019m ok with it because\u2026\u201d (Reasons could be \u201cI like the power\u201d or \u201cdemons are fallen angels, I focus on the angel not the fallen\u201d) and the Truth go \u201care my powers really because I\u2019m descended from the Devil?\u201d. How they treat monsters is unrelated to their Faction.<br /> <br /> Malleus Maleficarum: Merge The Order of St. Longinus and The Brotherhood of St. Athanasius into one group \u2013 but keep the conflict between them. Promote the Sisterhood of St. Wisdom to a primary group. Make witches and demons a larger priority than vampires; but I\u2019m fine with their Ghoul leader.<br /> <br /> Task Force: Valkyrie: I\u2019d like to see more focus on privileges. The ability to walk into any police department and tell them to hand everything over and delete the backups. The ability to arrest and interrogate anyone. I also think players need to be able to get access to a heavily armed black helicopter.<br /> <br /> Vampires should not be funding TFV. Vampires get to have secret control of hunter organisations that are introduced in the vampire books, not ones introduced in the Hunter books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T08:54:03-08:00","id":793119,"title":"","content":"Hey, I take offense at your slandering of Division Six! They're basically a poor man's Delta Green, and that's great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:10:13-08:00","id":793125,"title":"","content":"I haven't read Delta Green? Give me the low down.<br /> <br /> But to me it felt like most of it had already been done by TF:V, and the parts that hadn't didn't really work. I didn't think the technocracy references work once you reduce the technocracy's entire ethos down to killing reality devients, and you know I didn't like them being pawns of the Seers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:39:49-08:00","id":793149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=793125#post793125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read Delta Green? Give me the low down.<br /> <br /> But to me it felt like most of it had already been done by TF:V, and the parts that hadn't didn't really work. I didn't think the technocracy references work once you reduce the technocracy's entire ethos down to killing reality devients, and you know I didn't like them being pawns of the Seers.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the old-school fluff, Delta Green was formerly a government anti-supernatural task force that had been disavowed and forced underground. The members that still kept up the fight would tell new recruits that they were still working for the government until they had enough dirt on them to make sure they couldn't leave the conspiracy. That whole false legitimacy thing is super neat to me, as is being Seer pawns; I'd love to be jumped by a bunch of idiotic federal Sleepers in a Mage game.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of playing government Hunters that don't have super weapons or psychic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T12:40:37-08:00","id":793229,"title":"","content":"Hate to break it to you KR, but you missed one compact: Ahl al-Jabal. Great analysis otherwise, although I agree that Division 6 should stick around. I'm totally with you on Les Mysteres. <br /> <br /> Ahl Al-Jabal: these guys need to be in the corebook, and I'm not just saying that because they are my favourite or because I want to write them ass part of the open call. If we are looking at Hunter having a more global perspective, this compact is spot on for representing Ismaili Shia Muslims. I've read it to my girlfriend, who is Ismaili herself and she's amazed at how accurate they are to actual Ismaili beliefs. The only thing I'd change is I'd Suffism as a speciality they can take, and I really would like to see books stop using the word heresy when referring to Shiites unless we are going to start to refer to Anglecians and Protestants in the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T12:46:41-08:00","id":793233,"title":"","content":"Anything involving Sufi mystics is awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T12:54:27-08:00","id":793235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=793229#post793229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hate to break it to you KR, but you missed one compact</div> </div> </div> </div>???<br /> <br /> I missed a lot more than one.<br /> <br /> I like the Ahl Al-Jabal, though in 2E I would like to see some acknowledgement that they and the Ascending Ones (Knife of Paradise) are both Hashshashin. That is, the Ahl Al-Jabal are based on the actual historical Hashshashin while the Ascending Ones are based upon the myths about the Hashshashin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-26-2015, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T14:43:13-08:00","id":793274,"title":"","content":"I couldn't agree more with thekingsraven and loserman. <br /> <br /> I think the problem with Division Six is that they don't have a stand alone identity. They harken to mage the ascensions technocratic pogrom and they're explicitly made out to be pawns of the Exarchs. It feels like they were ported over from the world of darkness. There's nothing they do that hasn't been done before in say the Special Affairs Division and they don't really have a niche that isn't covered by TFV. In general I think that one of the problems in first edition was an overreliance on tying hunter conspiracies into various other supernatural setting material. <br /> <br /> Hinting at some greater connection is awesome, but I think hunter shines when it abandons the cannon of other chronicles of darkness games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T15:10:38-08:00","id":793282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpanishInquisition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=793274#post793274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't agree more with thekingsraven and loserman. <br /> <br /> I think the problem with Division Six is that they don't have a stand alone identity. They harken to mage the ascensions technocratic pogrom and they're explicitly made out to be pawns of the Exarchs. It feels like they were ported over from the world of darkness. There's nothing they do that hasn't been done before in say the Special Affairs Division and they don't really have a niche that isn't covered by TFV. In general I think that one of the problems in first edition was an overreliance on tying hunter conspiracies into various other supernatural setting material. <br /> <br /> Hinting at some greater connection is awesome, but I think hunter shines when it abandons the cannon of other chronicles of darkness games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my rebuttal. I've never play Ascension and never will. I love Division 6 and would miss them if they go. Tweek them to build more of their own niche? Sure. But don't scrap them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T16:59:29-08:00","id":793318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpanishInquisition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=793274#post793274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't agree more with thekingsraven and loserman. <br /> <br /> I think the problem with Division Six is that they don't have a stand alone identity. They harken to mage the ascensions technocratic pogrom and they're explicitly made out to be pawns of the Exarchs. It feels like they were ported over from the world of darkness. There's nothing they do that hasn't been done before in say the Special Affairs Division and they don't really have a niche that isn't covered by TFV. In general I think that one of the problems in first edition was an overreliance on tying hunter conspiracies into various other supernatural setting material. <br /> <br /> Hinting at some greater connection is awesome, but I think hunter shines when it abandons the cannon of other chronicles of darkness games.</div> </div> </div> </div>VALKYRIE is the United States' government's secret anti-supernatural military task force. They're equipped with darker-than-black Advanced Armory weapons, and are the best of the best from their home branches.<br /> <br /> Division Six is a tiny, underfunded conspiracy that thinks it works for the United States government. They have no special training or equipment, but think they're protecting their nation and the world.<br /> <br /> If you don't see a massive thematic difference there, you aren't looking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T21:53:42-08:00","id":793420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=792530#post792530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Null Mysteriis</b> doesn't need a conceptual shift, but it needs an attentive, science minded eye to look over its writeups, one that knows that science is a method, not the body of knowledge accumulated by the method. They shouldn't read like they rush into some science-fiction hypothesis to shoehorn their findings into before they have some solid foundation to ground it on. They should remember that &quot;I don't know&quot; is not a dirty word in science, and what's important isn't getting from no answer to an answer, but carefully chiselling at the edges of the unknown to make sure, however slowly the answer might have to come, it's one that fits the facts. A little pseudoscience presence is fine, both in the form of phenomena that are pseudoscience in the real world but real phenomena in the Chronicles of Darkness, and in the form of investigators who are a little kooky and don't quite have their reasoning straight. But the pseudoscientists need to feel like authentic pseudoscientists with systems based around foundational assumptions, not movie extras spouting a little bit of technobabble. A little more attention to what they use their findings for practically wouldn't hurt either, and is probably a good bridge to forge connections between the compact and other hunter cells and organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>My god agreed! Science is a method, and given that the Chronicles of Darkness exist in a world where things follow very strict rules (even if they aren't the real rules of physics) Null Mysteriis should be able to figure them out better than anyone else, rather than fall back on pulpy nonsense. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=793235#post793235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">???<br /> <br /> I missed a lot more than one.<br /> <br /> I like the Ahl Al-Jabal, though in 2E I would like to see some acknowledgement that they and the Ascending Ones (Knife of Paradise) are both Hashshashin. That is, the Ahl Al-Jabal are based on the actual historical Hashshashin while the Ascending Ones are based upon the myths about the Hashshashin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be okay with that if it were something like &quot;the myth of the Hashashin was partly inspired when the Ascending Ones were erroneously attributed to Ismailis of the Nizari State.&quot; I do not want to see them directly be Ismaili on more than the individual level. Ismailis have been levelled with the charge of being the descendants of &quot;The First Terrorists&quot; and drug lords because people believe in the stories of the Hashashin were true. No serious historical scholar believes that anymore, I have recently seen the idea called laughable in books and academic papers, and it is highly offensive to Ismailis. The Ahl Al-Jabal are an excellent example of how to respectfully and appropriately draw on those ideas in a non-offensive way, especially since the (false) idea of Ismaili hasish smokers is never alluded to. The Ascending Ones are supposed to date back to Egypt and have nothing that is uniquely Ismaili about them. Linking them without some major rewriting of the AO would be a step backwards (IMO, feel free to disagree).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T00:08:42-08:00","id":793461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=793420#post793420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be okay with that if it were something like &quot;the myth of the Hashashin was partly inspired when the Ascending Ones were erroneously attributed to Ismailis of the Nizari State.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more about the Steryotype section. With both groups having a steryotype of the other that says I'm the real deal and you're an imposter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=793420#post793420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Ascending Ones are supposed to date back to Egypt and have nothing that is uniquely Ismaili about them. Linking them without some major rewriting of the AO would be a step backwards (IMO, feel free to disagree).</div> </div> </div> </div>Their combat style is assassination (look at Elixirs like Crocodile Tears and Amun's Water). Their power comes from drugs. The Knife of Paradise is Islamic. That's the connection.<br /> <br /> Drug using Islamic assassins is basically the entirety of the myth about the Hashshashin. It's a myth, it's not really known for being rich in historical facts.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:18:34-08:00","id":793504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=793461#post793461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking more about the Steryotype section. With both groups having a steryotype of the other that says I'm the real deal and you're an imposter.</div> </div> </div> </div> That could work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their combat style is assassination (look at Elixirs like Crocodile Tears and Amun's Water). Their power comes from drugs. The Knife of Paradise is Islamic. That's the connection.<br /> <br /> Drug using Islamic assassins is basically the entirety of the myth about the Hashshashin. It's a myth, it's not really known for being rich in historical facts.<br /> </div> </div> </div> I know it's a myth. I'm saying that I also know fr working with the community the myth is about academically, and living with them personally, that said myth is considered racist. Onyx Path has made the very good habit of avoiding basing their material off such myths. I'd like to see that continue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 12-27-2015, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:10:49-08:00","id":793575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=793420#post793420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My god agreed! Science is a method, and given that the Chronicles of Darkness exist in a world where things follow very strict rules (even if they aren't the real rules of physics) Null Mysteriis should be able to figure them out better than anyone else, rather than fall back on pulpy nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that as written the NM theories can come across as obviously wrong and kinda silly. However; the real world runs on rules and people have trying to work them out for... well, since the beginnings of humanity probably, and we still don't have all the answers. Even in the traditionally defined era of the scientific method, it's been extremely hard to make progress. Hundreds of thousands of people have sunk their entire lives into advancing that body of knowledge only very slightly (and that's if they're lucky). That a small group such NM have made little progress is actually pretty realistic. Science is really hard.<br /> <br /> Also, the NM are going from a background of our modern materialist body of scientific knowledge, and then they encounter stuff that is totally out of left-field. There is literally no reason to suspect that there's an animistic Shadow to the world, and yet there it is. How do you even begin to theorise about it? That they end up flailing around trying desperately to make some sense of it within the frameworks they have shouldn't really be a surprise.<br /> <br /> I think there's an interesting tragedy to the group that gets lost by simply making them heroic scientists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:26:22-08:00","id":793585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/792501-compacts-conspiracies-the-great-reboot?p=793575#post793575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that as written the NM theories can come across as obviously wrong and kinda silly. However; the real world runs on rules and people have trying to work them out for... well, since the beginnings of humanity probably, and we still don't have all the answers. Even in the traditionally defined era of the scientific method, it's been extremely hard to make progress. Hundreds of thousands of people have sunk their entire lives into advancing that body of knowledge only very slightly (and that's if they're lucky). That a small group such NM have made little progress is actually pretty realistic. Science is really hard.<br /> <br /> Also, the NM are going from a background of our modern materialist body of scientific knowledge, and then they encounter stuff that is totally out of left-field. There is literally no reason to suspect that there's an animistic Shadow to the world, and yet there it is. How do you even begin to theorise about it? That they end up flailing around trying desperately to make some sense of it within the frameworks they have shouldn't really be a surprise.<br /> <br /> I think there's an interesting tragedy to the group that gets lost by simply making them heroic scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I totally agree! They'd be out of their depth in a lot of ways. The real world works off of consistent, reliable rules that can eventually be discerned. So do the Chronicles of Darkness. They may get a lot of things wrong, but may be able to discern some things, and at least have a grain of truth in others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:29:19-08:00","id":793589,"title":"","content":"I'm with Second Chances on this one.<br /> <br /> Wheather or not NM are making progress, there's a difference between not making progress and jumping to pulpy nonsense theories.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"